# Tests that pin what zeta does with PostgreSQL grammar and unsupported-feature probes sent over the MySQL wire.
# MySQL rejects most of it by design, so these are NOT judged against MySQL: they stay pinned to zeta's own output
# (their .result files are hand-maintained) and their agreement numbers are reported as a separate class.
# Format: path<TAB>reason. Every test not listed here is MySQL-targeted and needs an oracle record.
# Regenerate the membership with: ls tests/*/ | names starting pg_ (pg-grammar) or containing 'sentinel' (sentinel).
